From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HarnessOS <patches@harnessos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: render kind-neutral agent extensions and arm input safely

The kind-neutral agent-status source replaces upstream's per-kind branches, and
the titlebar test keeps its behavioural harness in place of the source-text
assertions upstream still carries; its OpenCode hook mock gained the
refreshLegacySharedPlugin call upstream makes at launch.

Carried-Because: Shared Pi and OMP homes must not depend on pane launch order; host-owned timers contain teardown and input preflight status.
Tests: src/main/pi/*test.ts; src/main/ipc/pty-spawn-env-agent-overlays.test.ts; src/main/ipc/pty-daemon-spawn-codex-auth.test.ts; src/main/ipc/pty-daemon-spawn-session-identity.test.ts

diff --git a/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md b/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md
index 249767d705adf6f4145e80812700fc47ed2c60ac..4b57fc29d1b04630dbfb8070dcc66f6d371cc97e 100644
--- a/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md
+++ b/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md
@@ -32,6 +32,14 @@ and Mac `orca-local-build.json` record the full workbench HEAD; environment comm
 overrides cannot replace it. HarnessOS publication additionally requires the exact
 artifact's signing and bind qualifications. A local build alone is not qualification.
 
+Pi and OMP can share `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`. Explicit agent launches install the
+same runtime-detecting status, prefill and titlebar templates into `agent/extensions/`;
+non-agent panes do not rewrite that directory. Files without Orca's managed marker
+remain user-owned. OMP's explicit status fallback is path-deduplicated by its loader,
+not content-deduplicated: a separate user copy can still produce duplicate events.
+The titlebar observes input before preflight, adopts that animation at agent start,
+and uses OMP's managed timers so shutdown cancels both animation and input expiry.
+
 ## Branch Naming
 
 Use a clear, descriptive branch name that reflects the change.
